#: includes/settings-fields/layout-collage.php:61
msgid "Templates, Grid and Random mosaic fill the Height; Random mosaic cuts it into places of different sizes, at random (Shuffle), shaped after their photos. Scattered: a photo in the middle and the others around it in uneven arms, each shaped after its photo, the gap between neighbours always the same; as large as the Height and the width allow, the corners left empty. Freeform: the photos at random places and sizes, a Gap apart, each then moved and resized by hand in the preview; all of it scales with the Height. Overlap: as Freeform, but the photos lie over one another, each on a layer of its own; placed by hand in the preview, the photo moved goes on top. With Height Auto, Freeform and Overlap fit their photos to the block (not the empty margins round them in the preview). Justified rows keep each photo’s proportions in rows across the width; Masonry in columns. Both are as tall as their photos make them; as a background, as tall as the block (the places stretched or shrunk to it)."
